{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Fix pushed for review — Gerrit change 2348\n\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2348 (commit `a36c9b8031cf`, branch\n`reb-a61d-proxy-redirect`). NOT submitted, NOT deployed; nginx on the box was not reloaded.\n\n### The change (+229 lines, 3 files)\n\n**`infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`** — `FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS: \"*\"` on `review-bot` and on\n`opcert`, the root-cause layer. Exactly the value and the bounded-trust reasoning the `mcp`\nservice already carries: `\"*\"` rather than a pinned bridge-gateway address because neither\nservice declares a `networks:` block, so that address is implicit and can drift; trust-all is\nbounded because both ports are published on host loopback with nginx the sole reachable client\nand nginx sets `X-Forwarded-Proto https` as a literal that overwrites client input.\n\n**`infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template`** — the structural backstop on all three surfaces\n(`/review/`, `/opcert/`, Gerrit `location /`), each block gaining:\n\n    proxy_redirect default;\n    proxy_redirect http://$host/          https://$host/;\n    proxy_redirect http://127.0.0.1:PORT/ https://$host/;\n\n**Per-location, never server-level** — 79b2's binding precedent, honoured. `proxy_redirect\ndefault;` is restated FIRST in every block, because nginx drops a location's implicit default the\nmoment any explicit rule appears there; that restatement is what preserves `/review/`'s\nprefix-stripping `default` rewrite (AC3), and the ordering matters because nginx evaluates rules\nin sequence.\n\n**`tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py`** — four new tests asserting on the RENDERED config\n(reusing 2333's `_render_nginx()` helper) and on the committed compose file.\n\n### AC status\n\n- **AC1** — established for all three, recorded in the RCA comment above. `/review/` and\n  `/opcert/` CAN emit (both reproduced); Gerrit CAN emit but does not downgrade\n  (`canonicalWebUrl = https://…`).\n- **AC2** — `test_nginx_upgrades_any_plaintext_location_on_the_sibling_surfaces`.\n- **AC3** — `test_nginx_sibling_surfaces_restate_the_default_proxy_redirect`, which asserts\n  `default` is present AND first.\n- **AC4** — `test_nginx_gerrit_location_still_has_no_rewrite_and_no_proxy_pass_path`, which pins\n  the reasoning (proxy_redirect touches only response headers) by failing if the backstop is ever\n  turned into a `rewrite` or a URI path is added to Gerrit's `proxy_pass`.\n- **AC5 (LIVE VALIDATION)** — **NOT met, and cannot be until this deploys.** It is the reason\n  this ticket stays `in_progress`. The current live headers are recorded in the RCA comment above\n  (the pre-fix state). Re-probe `/review/health/`, `/review/webhook/`, `/review/rerun/` and, with\n  a valid `X-Opcert-Guard`, `/opcert/jobs/` after the deploy and record the actual headers here.\n\n### Verification\n\n**nginx syntax** — the rendered config was parsed by real nginx (`nginx -t` in a throwaway\n`nginx:1.27-alpine` container, host-only externals stubbed): *syntax is ok / test is successful*.\n\n**Mutation check — 16 mutants, all killed** (`--color=no`, judged on the pytest return code, not\non stdout text). Deleting each of the three rules from each of the three blocks (9), moving\n`default` after the explicit rules in `/review/` and in Gerrit's block (2), adding a URI path to\nGerrit's `proxy_pass` (1), implementing the backstop as a `rewrite` (1), dropping\n`FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS` from each service (2), and pinning it to a bridge IP (1) each turn the\nsuite RED; restoring returns 52 passed.\n\n**A first mutation round found a real oracle defect and it was fixed, not accepted.** Two mutants\ninitially SURVIVED — dropping `proxy_redirect default;` from Gerrit's block, and reordering it in\n`/review/`. Cause: these blocks are heavily commented and the comments name the very directive\nunder test, so `re.findall(r\"proxy_redirect\\s+([^;]+);\", body)` matched the *prose* and the oracle\npassed on a config that no longer carried the rule. `_location_body()` now strips comment lines\nbefore scanning, and both mutants die.\n\n**Gates** — `make lint` clean; `make typecheck` clean (683 files); `pytest\ntests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` 4 passed; `check_complexity_baseline.py --check`\n`active=39 new=0 increased=0 stale=10`. `tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py` 52 passed; the\nwider related set (`test_mcp_on_box_infra` + `test_opcert_deploy_infra` + `test_review_bot` +\n`test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen`) 210 passed.\n\n### Deploy note (not actioned here)\n\n`autodeploy.sh`'s blue-green `mcp_run_new()` spells out the `mcp` service's env as `-e` flags and\nalready carries `FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS='*'` (`:380`). `review-bot` and `opcert` are started by\n`docker compose`, which reads the compose file directly, so no autodeploy change is needed for\nthem — but they DO need a container restart for the new env to take effect, and nginx needs a\nreload for the template change. Both happen on the next deploy."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787955444629920001,"uuid":"40e2cc91-65cd-48c1-bfdb-10d10a0dfd1e"}